    "realistic_degradation_finding": "When evaluated on a realistic day-disjoint split (training Mon-Wed, testing Thu-Fri), the supervised model encounters 5 attack classes (Bot, DDoS, Infiltration, PortScan, WebAttack) that did not exist in training. Rather than achieving 98-99% accuracy as seen in the repository's within-session split, the supervised classifier silently predicts a substantial fraction of OOD attacks as Benign (silent miss rate), or forces them into arbitrary known attack classes (DoS/BruteForce). Furthermore, Benign false alarms increase due to natural multi-day background drift. This proves that within-session split metrics (capture_group) are highly optimistic due to temporal leakage."
